number|title|condition|evidence|remediation|limitation|attack|nist|nist_rationale|sources|severity
001|A privileged account is stale by the approved definition|An enabled privileged account exceeds the approved inactivity threshold using sufficiently complete authoritative activity evidence.|Privileged membership; account state; domain/cloud activity coverage; approved threshold; owner exception.|Review and retire unused privileged access while preserving approved emergency accounts.|lastLogonTimestamp is replicated with delay and is not complete cloud activity. No activity data means Unknown.|T1078.002|AC-2;AC-6|Review account activity and remove unnecessary standing privilege.||Medium
002|Privileged access review is overdue|A defined privileged group or role has no current completed review within the approved cadence after owner confirmation.|Scoped roster; dated review evidence; approved cadence; owner attestation; outstanding actions.|Complete the access review and track decisions to closure.|Document discovery alone is not proof no review occurred. This check requires assisted evidence when no review system is integrated.|T1078|AC-2;AC-6|Maintain periodic review of privileged authorization.||Medium
003|An SPN remains attached to a retired service identity|Service-owner confirmation establishes retirement while an enabled account retains an SPN and unnecessary associated privilege.|SPN inventory; account state; service ownership and retirement evidence; effective grants.|Remove obsolete SPNs and retire or reduce the service account after dependency review.|Missing host inventory or old password age alone does not establish retirement.|T1558.003|AC-2;AC-6;CM-8|Keep service identities and privileges aligned with active service inventory.||Medium
004|A privileged service account lacks an accountable owner and review|A confirmed privileged service identity has no responsible owner or current review according to authoritative ownership records.|Service binding; effective privileges; ownership system; review requirement; owner escalation record.|Assign ownership and review the account's purpose, privileges, and credential management.|Do not classify every account without a description as ownerless; use the organization's actual system of record.|T1078.002|AC-2;AC-6;IA-5|Assign accountability for privileged service identities and their authenticators.||Medium
005|A domain controller machine-account password is outside policy|A live domain controller's machine-account password metadata exceeds the approved supported interval and no documented operational exception applies.|DC role/health; pwdLastSet metadata; replication state; approved interval and exception.|Investigate secure-channel and replication health and use supported recovery procedures.|Never reset DC passwords automatically. Old metadata may reflect replication or restored-state issues rather than compromise.|T1078.002|IA-5;SI-4|Monitor the lifecycle and health of domain-controller authentication.||Medium
006|A LAPS-managed credential is not rotating within policy|An active managed local account has rotation metadata outside its applicable configured policy and authorized collection covers its actual storage mode.|LAPS policy; expiration/rotation metadata; device health; storage mode; management errors.|Repair the approved credential rotation workflow and verify metadata afterward.|Do not read the credential. Offline devices and Entra-versus-AD storage require separate coverage treatment.|T1078.003|IA-5;SI-4|Maintain and monitor local administrator authenticator rotation.|MS-LAPS|Medium
007|Required certificate issuance auditing is absent|A confirmed in-scope CA lacks the effective audit settings or protected destination required by the approved certificate audit policy.|CA role; audit filter; effective Windows audit policy; destination; approved requirement.|Enable the required issuance and administration auditing and protect the records.|A CA template object alone does not reveal effective CA-host audit configuration.|T1649|AU-2;AU-9;AU-12|Keep certificate issuance and administration reviewable.|MDI-PKI|Medium
008|Required AD recovery backups lack current validation evidence|The approved forest recovery requirement lacks current successful backup or validation evidence confirmed by the backup owner.|Recovery scope; backup metadata; protected-copy inventory; last approved validation result; owner attestation.|Restore the required backup coverage and validate recovery in an isolated approved environment.|Backup existence is not restoration success. No backup-platform access is Unknown rather than Fail.|T1490|CP-9;CP-4;CP-10|Retain and validate recoverable copies of identity infrastructure.||High
